    "description": "What: CE-4692 BL-S1 (docs/designs/engineering/DESIGN_Bridge_Laying.md §5) — on basic-desert a RIVER (an authored Water feature, y 60-72 across the whole map) parts the south from the north. A LAID BRIDGE (an assault span, TKB 8825: a walkable-deck static obstacle, 18 m between its deck ends, 4 m wide, 1.2 m above the banks, a ramp at each end) is placed by the scenario at (80, 66), heading north, so its deck ends stand on the banks. Every node bakes it into its own terrain — the navmesh, the floor, sight and fire — before it is Open (held Constructing until the bake commits). 'Tank' (an M1 at (80, 20)) is ordered to (80, 110) on the far bank; 'Squad' (a leader and three riflemen at (64, 22)) marches to (64, 108). Judge: the tank reaches the far bank driving over the deck (up at deck height, never in the river beside it); the squad's objective 'reach the far bank' ends Achieved (all four men inside 15 m of (64, 108)). Fail: either stops at the river. Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh bl-placed-bridge"
